[188.026351, "i", "cat >> README.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Resume and durability\n\nEach checkpoint records the last committed document ID, document count, and byte\nlength of every committed shard. A commit flushes and fsyncs index data (including\nrotated shards) and the index directory, then fsyncs a temporary checkpoint and\natomically replaces `var/checkpoint.json`, fsyncing its directory as well.\n\nOn resume, the worker removes shards and truncates tails beyond those committed\nlengths before reading strictly *after* the last committed ID. This also recovers\nfrom SIGKILL during a write or between publishing data and its checkpoint. Missing\nor shortened committed shards fail closed instead of silently skipping documents.\nSIGTERM/SIGINT/SIGHUP request a stop after the current document and durable commit;\nif grace expires first, the same recovery protocol applies on the next run.\n\nPre-fix checkpoints have no shard offsets and cannot certify their buffered\noutput. They are rebuilt once, even if marked complete. Row transformations and\nthe JSON"]
[188.026918, "o", "cat >> README.md <<'EOF'\r\n\r\n## Resume and durability\r\n\r\nEach checkpoint records the last committed document ID, document count, and byte\r\nlength of every committed shard. A commit flushes and fsyncs index data (including\r\nrotated shards) and the index directory, then fsyncs a temporary checkpoint and\r\natomically replaces `var/checkpoint.json`, fsyncing its directory as well.\r\n\r\nOn resume, the worker removes shards and truncates tails beyond those committed\r\nlengths before reading strictly *after* the last committed ID. This also recovers\r\nfrom SIGKILL during a write or between publishing data and its checkpoint. Missing\r\nor shortened committed shards fail closed instead of silently skipping documents.\r\nSIGTERM/SIGINT/SIGHUP request a stop after the current document and durable commit;\r\nif grace expires first, the same recovery protocol applies on the next run.\r\n\r\nPre-fix checkpoints have no shard offsets and cannot certify their buffered\r\noutput. They are rebuilt once, even if marked complete. Row transformat"]
[188.027004, "i", "-lines format are unchanged. As before, this is a reindex of a stable\nsource corpus; use `./jobs clean` to explicitly start a new pass after source changes.\nEOF\npython3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path('tests/test_durability.py')\ns = p.read_text().replace('import json\\n', '')\np.write_text(s)\nPY\n"]
[188.027016, "o", "ions and\r\nthe JSON-lines format are unchanged. As before, this is a reindex of a stable\r\nsource corpus; use `./jobs clean` to explicitly start a new pass after source changes.\r\nEOF\r\npython3 - <<'PY'\r\nfrom pathlib import Path\r\np = Path('tests/test_durability.py')\r\ns = p.read_text().replace('import json\\n', '')\r\np.write_text(s)\r\nPY\r\n"]
